@startuml sequence-diagram-4

' Sheet 4/4 - A4 portrait. See sequence-diagram.puml for the whole diagram.
skinparam dpi 200
scale max 1500*2150

title node-sso-consumer - WSS authentication and realtime delivery of ME\nSheet 4/4: the other ways a session ends, and the reconnection

autonumber 57

actor "User" as User

participant "Front Application\nBrowser" as Browser
participant "SSO Client\nnode-sso-consumer/client" as Client
participant "Node Application\nnode-sso-consumer" as App
participant "Realtime Bridge\nnode-sso-consumer" as Bridge
participant "x-core\nSSO / Realtime Provider" as XCore


note over User, XCore #LightYellow
CONTINUED FROM SHEET 3/4:
me-changed is the nominal case. Here are the four others.
end note


group "Ticket valid" branch (continued)

    == 11. The other ways a session ends ==

    alt me-signed-out frame { data: true }

        XCore --> Bridge : me-signed-out
        Bridge --> Client : me-signed-out
        Client -> Client : ended()

        note right of Client
        IdP session closed, account disabled,
        or access to this application revoked.
        end note

    else me-sessions frame

        XCore --> Bridge : me-sessions [ ... ]
        Bridge --> Client : me-sessions [ ... ]
        Client -> Client : readOwnSession(data)

        opt The "current" row went AFTER having been seen

            Client -> App : GET /api/auth/session
            App --> Client : 401, or a ME
            Client -> Client : ended() if refused or not admitted

            note over Client, App
            THE ONLY HTTP read after the connection,
            and it is not on a timer.

            It is the one way of ending a session that
            me-signed-out does not report: ending ONE session
            from the sign-ins screen moves neither the IdP
            session nor the account's access.

            Rotation replaces the row every 15 minutes:
            a frame read in the gap shows no row of ours
            while the session is alive. Hence the confirmation.
            end note
        end

    else x-core closes the socket

        XCore --> Bridge : close 4001 / 4002 / 4003
        Bridge --> Client : close 4001 / 4002 / 4003\ncode passed through untouched
        Client -> Client : ended(), no reconnection

        note right of Client
        The code travels through the Bridge intact: without it,
        the client cannot tell a session that is over
        from a plain transport failure.
        end note

    else Network drop

        Client -> Client : Reconnection, backoff 1s -> 30s
        Client -> App : POST /api/auth/realtime-ticket\na FRESH ticket on every dial

        note right of Client
        Also woken by online, focus and visibilitychange,
        without waiting out the backoff: coming back to a tab
        is exactly when a stale page is in front
        of somebody.
        end note
    end


    == 12. The connection carries on ==

    ... waiting for the next event ...

    XCore --> Bridge : me-changed { new SsoMe }
    Bridge --> Client : me-changed { new SsoMe }
    Client -> Client : onAccount(me)

end

@enduml
